id: pm-gh1773
title: "GH-1773: refusal envelopes echo URL userinfo when it contains whitespace and a percent-encoded @ separator"
description: "GH-1773 (filed 2026-11-23 from the pm-rust parity review, reproduced on the pinned pm-cli oracle; native and TS behave the same). A refusal envelope echoes an open blocker's title verbatim. When that title holds a URL whose userinfo contains whitespace and a percent-encoded @ (https://fixture:fake words%40example.invalid/path), the userinfo is not masked: pm start-task sample-one --json refused by that blocker prints 'fixture:fake words'. Expected: credential-shaped URL userinfo is masked in every refusal and diagnostic projection, whitespace-bearing userinfo and an encoded separator included, matching the masking of plain user:pass@host; plain masking unchanged. Duplicate check: searched redaction URL userinfo whitespace percent-encoded separator refusal envelope; pm-gh1707 (closed) fixed public-URL @-in-path over-redaction and claim-refusal echoes, pm-nhauur and pm-5htunt (closed) cover other echo surfaces, none covers whitespace plus encoded separators."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,"gh:1773",privacy,redaction,security
created_at: "2026-11-23T17:23:25.235Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-24T05:55:06.245Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-24T00:09:48.145Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-24T00:09:48.145Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "A redaction corpus case covers whitespace in userinfo with a percent-encoded separator, applied to refusal envelopes, diagnostics and JSON and TOON output; Plain user:pass@host masking and public URLs with @ in the path are unchanged"
parent: pm-qwoy
risk: medium
confidence: high
reporter: unbraind
severity: medium
resolution: "redactUrlCredentialsInText now joins a URL whose userinfo holds blanks into one word before the word rule runs: a word opens a join at the last scheme separator that authority slashes follow when its authority holds a non host:port colon, or is a single label whose password colon comes later (never a clock time; a colon that a space follows only before a host with a path or inside a URL its quote closes), or ends with its slashes (a tab follows); it is joined through the later word holding the authority's last at sign or its escape within 16 words and 512 code units, stops at another URL, a path delimiter or the URL's closing delimiter, and the joined span is redacted exactly as the same URL without blanks. Windows drives, Markdown links, quoted URLs and public host-and-port prose stay intact. The start-task refusal from the issue now prints only the scheme, the placeholder and the host in JSON and text output. Review: Codex rounds 1 to 5, Greptile rounds 1 to 4 and CodeRabbit round 1 addressed; residuals recorded on pm-jcz7qz."
expected_result: "Credential-shaped URL userinfo is masked in every refusal and diagnostic projection whatever whitespace or encoding it carries, and plain user:pass@host masking is unchanged"
actual_result: "The issue reproduction, the plain at-sign variant and every review-round leak are masked idempotently; plain masking and public URLs with an at sign in the path are unchanged, and prose cases stay intact"
dependencies[4]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
