comments[16]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-23T21:44:48.289Z","harness:claude-code","Root cause and fix (2026-11-23): redactUrlCredentialsInText judged each whitespace-delimited word alone, so a stored title holding a URL whose password contains a blank split into a scheme word with a colon but no at sign and a host word with an at sign (or its percent escape) but no colon; neither word matched the token rule. The plain at-sign form leaked the same way, not only the encoded one, and Node's WHATWG URL parser reads that spelling as userinfo with a spaced password. Fix in src/core/shared/url-credentials.ts: before the word rule, a word with no at sign that opens a URL authority with a user-colon prefix (scheme, one or two slashes, a colon that port digits alone never follow, no path, no bracketed IPv6 host) is joined across any whitespace with the later words up to the first that holds an at sign or its escape, within 16 words and 512 code units and before another URL starts, and the joined span goes through redactUrlCredentialsInToken. Line breaks and tabs count as blanks because URL parsers drop them. Host-and-port and plain-host prose before a later at sign stays intact. Every outbound surface (refusal guidance in JSON and text, telemetry sanitizeString, Sentry scrubbing) already routes free text through this one function. Verified end to end in a sandbox: a start-task refusal gated by such a blocker now prints the scheme, the placeholder and the host only, in JSON and TOON output."
  "2026-11-23T22:40:06.039Z","harness:claude-code","Rework after Codex review round 1 (2026-11-23, 8 URL findings). The opening word may now hold its own separator (an encoded at sign inside the password), skips any number of authority slashes, ignores a colon that only appears in a query or fragment, exempts only a real host:port head (a label run, a colon and at least one digit), and also opens on a single dotless label when a later word carries the user-password colon (a spaced username). The continuation takes the LAST at sign or its escape that starts within 16 words and 512 code units, as a URL parser takes the authority's last at sign; the word holding it may run past the length bound (a long query), and a word that starts another URL or holds a path delimiter before any separator ends the search. All 8 reproductions are pinned in tests/unit/core/shared/url-credentials.spec.ts, and the earlier prose and bound cases still pass."
  "2026-11-23T22:56:20.809Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 2 (2026-11-23): a redirect URL in the final word's query stopped the scan before its separator (now only a scheme at the end of the text before the first path delimiter starts another URL, read back from the colon, which also removes the quadratic unanchored scheme search Codex measured); a dotted spaced username and a password starting with digits were not joined (any colon-bearing head that is no dotted or localhost host:port now opens, and a dotless or dotted label opens when a later word carries a colon with text after it); a quoted URL followed by prose with a colon was over-redacted (a quote, backtick or angle bracket in the authority ends it). Declined with reason: preserving the host and path after a join — the single-token rule masks through the last at sign by design (GH-1707, base64 passwords hold slashes), and the joined span is pinned to redact exactly as the same URL without blanks."
  "2026-11-23T22:58:26.252Z","harness:claude-code","Greptile review round 1 (2026-11-23, P1): a tab right after the authority slashes split the URL before its username, so no opening word was found and the spaced password survived. A word that ends with its authority slashes is now a pending opening whose authority starts in the next word, judged as if the blank between them were dropped (URL parsers drop tabs and line breaks there); prose with a bare scheme is still left alone."
  "2026-11-23T23:10:34.962Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 3 and Greptile round 2 (2026-11-24): the scheme separator is the first colon that authority slashes follow, so a compact JSON field name before the URL is skipped; a quote, backtick or angle bracket ends the URL only when it directly precedes the scheme (an apostrophe inside a password is data); a label opening may hold percent escapes (only an at sign or its escape is excluded); a password colon that a tab or line break follows counts, a clock time never does, and a colon that a space follows counts only when the separator's host goes on into a path (URL-shaped, never an email address); an encoded at sign that starts inside the 512-unit bound is read whole; the host:port check runs only on a DNS-length head, so an 8M-character dotted host no longer overflows the regex stack inside the redactor."
  "2026-11-23T23:25:21.666Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 4 (2026-11-24): fixed a pathless redirect query hiding the separator (another URL starts only when its scheme opens the word, optionally after one opening quote or bracket), a quoted pathless URL with a spaced password colon (the closing quote bounds it), and a regression where a Windows drive path joined through an error code to a mention (a one-letter scheme is a drive, never a URL). Exotic spellings recorded as residuals (22) to (25) on pm-jcz7qz."
  "2026-11-23T23:36:58.172Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 5 (2026-11-24): a credential URL nested in a public URL's query is now judged (the opening uses the last scheme separator in the word, and the joined span is redacted as the token rule redacts the same text without blanks); a Markdown link destination or any URL in parentheses or square brackets ends at its closing bracket, so a link followed by prose with a colon and a mention is no longer over-redacted (a regression against main). Split-username, bracketed-username and non-special backslash spellings recorded as residuals (26) and (27) on pm-jcz7qz."
  "2026-11-23T23:56:41.186Z","harness:claude-code","Greptile review round 3 (2026-11-24): a numeric username part (123:pass) and an empty password (a colon right before the at sign) are now joined, because only clock-shaped words (09:30, 12:30Z, 9:30pm) are kept apart; a closing parenthesis or square bracket ends a URL only at the end of a word followed by punctuation at most, so one inside a password is data while Markdown link destinations still end at their bracket."
  "2026-11-24T00:39:23.671Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit review round 2 (2026-11-24, after close, on 30bc2a4a9): a pending opening (the scheme slashes, a tab, then a word holding the whole userinfo) skipped past the word that held the separator, so a token-shaped username stayed visible; that word now seeds the join end, and a later separator still extends it."
  "2026-11-24T01:40:00.253Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit review round 3 (2026-11-24): only a WHATWG special scheme ends the authority at a slash or backslash; any other scheme (ssh, git+ssh) reads spaced userinfo across slashes, as OpenSSH reads a slash-bearing username, so a spaced SSH username or password holding a slash is masked while an ordinary HTTP path still stays out of the join."
  "2026-11-24T01:54:13.206Z","harness:claude-code","Greptile review round 8 (2026-11-24): making the SSH authority read across slashes also cleared the path-after-host signal, so an SSH URL with a spaced password colon before a host with a path stayed split. The path after the separator's host is now judged on its own, apart from whether a slash ends the search; pinned."
  "2026-11-24T02:58:56.820Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit review round 4 (2026-11-24, major): a Windows drive path inside spaced SSH userinfo was read as another URL and stopped the join; a one-letter scheme is now never another URL in the continuation scan either. Pinned."
  "2026-11-24T03:53:05.732Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit review round 5 (2026-11-24, major): a pending opening (scheme slashes, a tab, then the authority) was rejected by the special-scheme path check when the authority word went on into a path, exposing a token username; the pending authority is now judged up to its path delimiter, and the SSH variant (no path check) is pinned too."
  "2026-11-24T04:07:27.419Z","harness:claude-code","Greptile review round 10 (2026-11-24): after the path-bearing pending fix, a tab-split public link with a path searched later prose and over-redacted through a mention; a path in the authority word after the tab now ends the authority there, so only that word is joined when it holds a separator and later prose is never searched."
  "2026-11-24T04:54:53.043Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit review round 6 (2026-11-24, 2 major): a colon and slash inside SSH userinfo was read as a nested scheme, and an SSH username holding a query or fragment mark was cut there before classification. A later scheme separator now opens a nested URL only when its scheme starts the word or follows a query, fragment or opening character, and only a special scheme's authority ends at a query or fragment mark. Pinned."
  "2026-11-24T05:55:06.245Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit review round 7 (2026-11-24, major and minor): a quoted tab-split pending authority now ends at the delimiter that opened the URL, so a token username is masked; and a special scheme's authority ends at a query or fragment mark in both the opening word and the continuation scan, so a public link with a query or fragment never joins later prose through a mention. Pinned."
